  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R3", "R4"],
      "pins": ["R3.1", "R3.2", "J3.3", "R4.1", "R4.2"],
      "nets": ["/PWM1", "Net-(J3-Pin_3)", "/PWM2", "Net-(J8-Pin_3)"],
      "observed": "R3, the series resistor feeding the channel-1 servo signal (J3 pin 3) from /PWM1, has value \"1M\" (SPICE: `R3 Net-_J3-Pin_3_ /PWM1 1Meg`), while its counterpart R4 on channel 2 is \"1k\". Both carry the same LCSC code (C21190), so they are meant to be the same part.",
      "expected": "The specification states R3 and R4 are '1k each' series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3. R3 should be 1k, matching R4.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R3\")\n      (value \"1M\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R4\")\n      (value \"1k\")"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R3 Net-_J3-Pin_3_ /PWM1 1Meg"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."}
      ],
      "impact": "With a 1 MΩ series resistor instead of 1 kΩ, the channel-1 PWM signal at J3 pin 3 is severely attenuated/edge-slowed (high-impedance servo input + 1 MΩ forms a large RC), so the pan servo driven from J3 will likely not receive a valid PWM signal and PWM mode is effectively broken on channel 1 only.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design matches the specification except for R3, the channel-1 PWM series resistor, which is populated as 1M instead of the specified 1k (R4 on channel 2 is correctly 1k), a value that would prevent servo channel 1 from receiving a proper PWM signal."
}

